{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ll frame the aggregate gains alongside benchmark-specific reversals, without attributing them to untested components.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$(cat)\"; }\napply_patch <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Score-Targeted Subsets for Predicting LLM Benchmark Accuracy\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"How accurately can a source-trained, score-targeted shared item subset and decoder predict retained full-benchmark accuracy and model rankings at 5-, 10-, and 25-item budgets, relative to local benchmark-estimation baselines, and where does the comparison reverse?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On nine frozen benchmark matrices, the evaluated score-targeted acquisition-and-decoding package has lower average accuracy-prediction error than the recorded baselines when averaging equally over benchmarks, seeds, and query budgets, but its advantage over local IRT is not uniform across benchmarks and does not establish the benefit of any individual decoder component or transfer beyond this snapshot.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation of one frozen package against paired, budget-matched local estimators, including an evaluator-provided lineage-block uncertainty analysis. The independent qualification sources report completed and qualified; no downstream_study is present. Aggregate candidate MAE is 0.038991605535293065, compared with local IRT 0.05911223215296765 and uniform sampling 0.10520541810011626. The IRT paired MAE-difference interval excludes zero conditional on the fixed cases, while the raw case-by-budget predictions reveal reversals in math, legalbench, and med_qa. These reversals are part of the thesis, not inconvenient supplementary-only results. Prefer one shared estimation question with condition-specific evidence blocks for the leaderboard and HELM matrices, not separate chronological experiments. Reject a random-audit unbiasedness paper because that is not the final evaluated package; reject a nonlinear-decoder superiority paper because activation and isolated component effects are unverified; reject a universal or adaptive-evaluation story because the evaluated item path is source-only and shared across targets. The empirical framing is ready, but the supplied bibliography needs task-relevant, permitted-source repair before a defensible final related-work section can be written.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"This is fresh framing, not an enabled manuscript-edit pass: no resolved edit-context file, previous_paper manuscript, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory is supplied here. The recentered label describes narrowing the broad source-task brief to the frozen evaluated package and its heterogeneous accuracy, not a claim to have revised an unseen prior manuscript. Preserve-only framing has no prior text to justify; broadening to a shared adaptive or cross-setting method family is unsupported; recentering on the final paired evidence is strongest. Do not inherit a title or figure plan from private memory.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation, read independently of the absent downstream_study, supplies nine distinct final cases, three seeds, three query budgets, paired baseline predictions, and qualification facts. It changes the center of gravity from broad method search to a frozen-package comparison.\\\",\n+    \\\"Direct inspection of results/ideas/03_log_odds_shift_residual_decoder/program_1/src/program.py, surrogate.py, and nonlinear_decoder.py establishes a common score-covariance item path, all-query ridge/offset decoding, and a source-selected optional log-odds/residual branch with an incumbent fallback. The source tree is the local counterpart identified by the frozen selection manifest; no candidate was executed in this stage. No per-case selected branch is attested by the final evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"task/evaluate_final.py and task/resources/final/*_manifest.json clarify group-weighted errors, lineage-mean ranking, equal-case aggregation, replay exclusion, local baseline definitions, content reconciliation, and metadata-limited lineage separation. They prevent claims about universally independent models or every original benchmark item.\\\",\n+    \\\"Diagnostic postprocessing of final raw predictions, excluding replay and using lineage-equal weights, identifies local IRT reversals: math at all budgets, legalbench at 5 and 25, and med_qa at 10 and 25. These derived diagnostic signs determine the main figure plan; exact plotted values must be regenerated from the same records, not copied from rounded diagnostics.\\\",\n+    \\\"No ablation studies or previously generated figures are supplied. The earlier estimator implementations are development-only context, not mandatory main-paper groups or controlled component ablations. No new experiments are prerequisites for this bounded comparison story.\\\",\n+    \\\"VENUE.md and paper.sty require an anonymized ICLR 2026 single-column paper with 5.5-inch text width, 9-inch text height, and an 8-to-9-page body. The figure plan therefore uses full-text-width placement, not two-column assumptions.\\\",\n+    \\\"references.bib and references_provenance.json contain mostly off-topic retrievals; reference_retrieval.log shows the quota was exhausted before the planned LLM-specific title queries. Existing metadata is not evidence that relevant literature was read. No retrieval, citation-network browsing, or prohibited-literature identification was attempted during framing.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Score-targeted acquisition and source-selected score decoding\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"This is the frozen final package: lineage-weighted source response/score covariance, regularized conditional-gain selection with one representative per content group, a nested common subset, and all-observation decoding. Explain linear ridge/offset and optional log-odds plus residual ridge as implemented alternatives within the package; do not claim the optional branch was active or responsible for the measured gain.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Uniform content-group sampling\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Recorded, budget-matched simple comparator. The local implementation samples distinct content-group representatives, accounts for group mass, and clips its estimate; describe this rather than silently substituting an ordinary unweighted item mean.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Source-score prior\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Recorded no-target-response reference quantifies what can be predicted from source scores alone; its observation cost is zero even when displayed beside the other methods at each budget.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Response-vector anchors\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Recorded source-response representative selection and cluster-weighted averaging contextualize a structurally different acquisition/estimation family. The local normalized-response, farthest-first implementation is not an attested reproduction of the published Anchor Points method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Local Rasch-style IRT estimator\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The strongest recorded aggregate comparator and the essential reference for heterogeneous failures. It uses source-fitted item difficulty, the same uniform query path as the uniform baseline, and queried-response target-ability fitting. It is not the complete tinyBenchmarks system or an exhaustive tuned IRT comparison.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary estimand: full mean binary accuracy over the retained, reconciled item matrix, not necessarily the original unfiltered benchmark. Primary error is target-lineage-equal MAE, then equally averaged across the declared budgets, seeds, and nine cases. Source and target model-lineage group assignments are disjoint under the supplied metadata policy, not under a proved complete ancestry relation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main aggregate table: selected package MAE 0.038991605535293065 and RMSE 0.04837892636321264; local IRT MAE 0.05911223215296765; uniform 0.10520541810011626; source prior 0.08335016635136305; anchors 0.15674229873896958. Ground every reported final metric in final.metric.* and keep raw score units in [0,1]. Do not imply these averages are specifically 25-item results.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main paired uncertainty view: candidate-minus-IRT MAE -0.02012062661767458, recorded 95% interval [-0.02570984836073398, -0.014632649205711504]. Also show the recorded paired differences and intervals against uniform, prior, and anchors. The 200-draw lineage-block bootstrap retains seeds and budgets within groups and conditions on the fixed nine cases; the identical interval repeated in each seed wrapper is one aggregate analysis, not three independent intervals.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main heterogeneity view: all nine cases at each budget, expressed as paired candidate-minus-local-IRT MAE with a common zero reference. Preserve math losses at every budget, legalbench reversals at 5 and 25, and med_qa reversals at 10 and 25. Do not infer causes from ecosystem membership, source count, or benchmark names. Any case-specific interval would require a documented new postprocessing analysis; the supplied aggregate interval cannot be reused as a per-case interval.\\\",\n+    \\\"Ranking is a distinct outcome, not an inferred consequence of MAE: final Spearman 0.8158480130897703 and Kendall 0.6715966634525837 are calculated on lineage-mean predictions/truth and then averaged by the evaluator. Do not concatenate models from different benchmarks into one correlation. Baseline ranking cells may be filled only by a reproducible extraction from existing baseline predictions with exactly the same rules; otherwise show not reported, not zero, and make no ranking-superiority claim.\\\",\n+    \\\"Robustness/control reporting: recorded permuted-source MAE 0.06257521756337783 and zero-response-control MAE 0.21577661527598374 concern interventions on the same package. Constant refers to zeroed target observations in the protocol, not necessarily a constant predictor; permuted refers to independent row-wise circular shifts of source columns. These are sensitivity checks, not isolated ablations or proof of the mechanism, validity, or absence of contamination.\\\",\n+    \\\"Search and final are different evidence scopes: development uses arc_challenge, ifeval, commonsense, and gsm with seeds 101 and 211; final uses bbh, gpqa, mmlu_pro, musr, openllm_math, legalbench, math, med_qa, and mmlu with seeds 1009, 2003, and 3001. No pooled search/final table, before/after gain, cross-variant significance, search-score delta, or attempt-loss rate is planned. No study.* namespace exists here to support a downstream campaign accounting analysis.\\\",\n+    \\\"Preserve original-comparator honesty: the initial anchor/ridge implementation is readable under task/program_0 but has no matched final measurements in this bundle; omit a quantitative original-program comparison rather than borrowing an incumbent score from memory. Retain the four actual recorded final comparators. No controlled ablation bundle exists.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: historical source responses and full source scores produce one common score-targeted item path; a new target contributes only queried answers to a source-selected decoder; complete retained target scores are used solely for external evaluation. Distinguish source fitting, legal target observation, and scoring by labeled lanes and a visual information boundary. Mark optional nonlinear decoding as source-selected, not as an experimentally established mechanism.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, aggregate paired comparison: a horizontal forest plot of candidate-minus-baseline MAE for the four recorded baselines, using the one supplied aggregate lineage-block interval per comparator and a zero line. A nearby compact table carries absolute errors and separately identified ranking results.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, scope and reversals: two vertically stacked dot-plot panels, one with the five leaderboard cases and one with the four HELM cases; within each case show the three budget-specific candidate-minus-local-IRT MAEs using displaced symbols, not connected progression curves. A common signed x-axis exposes local losses as well as gains.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"score_prediction_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the estimation target, shared score-directed subset, source-selected decoder, and target-truth information boundary legible at a glance.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"information_role\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none_conceptual_information_flow\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"none\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected paper.sty sets one 5.5-inch-wide column and 9-inch text height. Use the full 5.5-inch text width, about 2.0 inches of drawing height plus a short caption, early on page 2; a half-width figure would make matrix labels and the training/evaluation boundary too small. Allocate about 0.30 body page including caption. Use one panel, at most six labeled blocks, and at least 9-point rendered labels.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"paired_error_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show the signed aggregate error difference and conditional uncertainty against every recorded baseline without equating average gains with universal wins.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"forest_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"baseline_method\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"candidate_minus_baseline_mae_with_recorded_95_percent_interval\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"none_equal_case_budget_seed_aggregate\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use the single-column 5.5-inch text width and about 1.7 inches of axes height, with four comparator rows and one point/interval per row. The full span preserves readable comparator names, signed ticks, and a zero reference at 9-point or larger type. Place near the aggregate results, around page 6; budget about 0.26 body page including caption. Do not squeeze it into a hypothetical two-column slot or truncate interval endpoints.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 1\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"case_budget_reversals\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose budget-specific benchmark heterogeneity, including where the selected package loses to the strongest recorded aggregate baseline.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"faceted_horizontal_dot_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"benchmark\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"candidate_minus_local_irt_mae\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"data_ecosystem_with_budget_symbols\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"At the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width, stack the five-case and four-case panels vertically in one column rather than shrinking nine case labels into adjacent mini-panels. Target about 3.2 inches total axes height, one shared signed x-scale, three offset symbols per case for 5/10/25 items, and labels at least 9 points. Place around page 7 and budget about 0.43 body page including caption. Use labels or shapes as well as color; never suppress positive differences or connect points as a search trajectory.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 5,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Supply reimplementation, auditability, and complete evidence disaggregation after the references while keeping aggregate uncertainty, benchmark reversals, and the principal limitations in the main paper; no proposed experiment is presented as completed.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Weighted Acquisition and Decoder Specification\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand the weighted covariance definitions, conditional squared score-covariance over regularized conditional item variance, content-group exclusion, ridge/offset prediction, and optional penalized log-odds/full-population curve/residual-ridge equations. Transcribe the implemented tuning shortlists, fold construction, clipping, zero-budget fallback, and insufficient-group/allowance fallback from the inspected selected src/surrogate.py and src/nonlinear_decoder.py. Treat component behavior as code specification, not measured ablation evidence. The final evidence and frozen tree metadata link this specification to the studied package.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Frozen Data and Lineage/Content Provenance\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the pinned benchmark-prediction snapshot, task/resources/rebuild.py, retained columns, source/target row and item-group policies, and file hashes in task/resources/final/*_manifest.json. Reconcile dimensions with the evaluated arrays rather than generic counts from the task brief. Include metadata-limited ancestry and conservative common-stem limitations; these also receive a concise main-text disclosure. Do not expose model identities or file paths as a substitute for scientific grouping definitions.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Benchmark, Budget, and Seed Results\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate every non-replay normal case/budget/seed result from final raw predictions for the selected package and four recorded baseline prediction arrays. Compute lineage-equal MAE and the evaluator-defined ranking summaries reproducibly, reconcile the primary aggregates to final.metric.*, and retain all loss cells. Identify any newly derived baseline RMSE or ranking statistics as postprocessing of existing predictions, not new experimental runs. Do not invent intervals for individual cells.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.rmse\\\", \\\"final.metric.spearman\\\", \\\"final.metric.kendall\\\", \\\"final.metric.irt_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.uniform_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.anchor_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.prior_mae\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Paired Uncertainty and Observation Controls\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Explain the single recorded 200-draw, fixed-case, lineage-block bootstrap, retention of checkpoints/seeds within groups, equal-case averaging, and treatment of missing cells in the evaluator policy. Report the actual recorded zero failed normal cells, without converting it into a performance success rate. Expand normal, zeroed-target-observation, source-column-shift, duplicate-history, and deterministic-replay definitions from task/evaluate_final.py. Keep control behavior distinct from full validity certification and do not count the BBH replay as another benchmark.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.constant_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.permuted_mae\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Reproduction and Evidence Boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Provide anonymized data reconstruction and evaluation commands based on the inspected scripts, available requirement/specification files, artifact hashes, exact recorded seeds and budgets, and a table mapping each final table/figure to its eventual extraction script and source records. Commands not rerun by the writer must be labeled as such. Describe CPU requirements as requirements, not measured speedups; give no unmeasured end-to-end runtime. Preserve final completed/qualified outcome separately from search feedback, and record the absence of controlled ablations and per-case decoder-selection diagnostics.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented use of LLM agents for research ideation, candidate implementation, reference-query planning, paper framing, and eventual writing/figure assistance, distinguishing these roles from evaluator-produced measurements. Identify verification actually performed rather than inventing human review. Document that framing performed local artifact inspection and prediction postprocessing only, not candidate execution or additional experiments. Track any later literature incident truthfully without guessing the prohibited work's identity.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Iteration History\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"From Audit to Ridge to Nonlinear\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Configuration\\\",\n+    \\\"Nonlinear Decoder Ablation\\\",\n+    \\\"Universal Benchmark Prediction\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\",\n+    \\\"wins on every benchmark\\\",\n+    \\\"proves generalization\\\",\n+    \\\"leakage-free\\\",\n+    \\\"the nonlinear component caused the gain\\\",\n+    \\\"unbiased rankings\\\",\n+    \\\"adaptive per-target acquisition\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Plan an approximately 8.5-page ICLR 2026 body including figures/tables, excluding references and substantive Supplementary Information. Allocate 1.5 pages to title/abstract/introduction plus the early overview; 1.0 to problem/estimand and focused related work; 1.8 to acquisition, decoding and source-only tuning; 1.1 to frozen protocol/data/baseline definitions; 2.0 to aggregate uncertainty, ranking and case/budget reversals; and 1.1 to limitations, interpretation and conclusion. If the body ends at eight pages, the final body page must be at least 75% full; never exceed nine body pages. Use available space for equations, definitions and evidence interpretation, not padding or a run diary.\\\",\n+    \\\"Suggested thesis-first headings: Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Score-Targeted Subset Prediction; Evaluation Protocol; Aggregate Accuracy and Conditional Uncertainty; Benchmark-Specific Reversals and Ranking; Scope and Limitations; Conclusion. Results subsections may share one top-level Results heading. Put substantive Supplementary Information after references; include a separate LLM Usage section there.\\\",\n+    \\\"Qualification is independently grounded in final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, and final.qualification.correct=true. Do not derive qualification from a search score, remembered acceptance statement, or publication readiness. Do not claim unseen gate diagnostics establish adaptivity, generalization, or complete validity. If a later authoritative evaluation changes the outcome, preserve that outcome and any reported limitations throughout writing, review, audit, and revision; missing causes stay unknown.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use final.metric.* for final numbers and final.evidence.episodes for paired analyses. There are no study.* sources and no downstream_study; omit search-score differences and scored/unscored accounting rather than reconstructing them from private memory. Never treat an unscored attempt as a measured loss. Report no inherited original-program metric without matched evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only artifact identifiers, hashes, result.* search fields, and internal selection labels belong in evidence bookkeeping, not titles, abstract, tables, or visible metrics. Refer to the frozen package, model variants, query budgets, and recorded evaluation. Source identifiers listed in this strategy are audit anchors, not literal paper prose.\\\",\n+    \\\"All figure spans refer to the actual one-column 5.5-inch text width in paper.sty: column width and full text width coincide here. Do not use figure* or 0.48-width two-column defaults. Respect the per-figure height, label and panel budgets; at most two total panels are needed and no figure has more than one panel per row. Prefer a page-2 overview to adding a dense late appendix architecture diagram.\\\",\n+    \\\"Only score_prediction_overview uses generate-concept-figure; the downstream orchestrator owns that pipeline, and this stage only plans it. Require an editable diagram source and deterministic faithful export; do not fabricate illustrative outcome values or imply active nonlinear decoding. Quantitative figures use source-controlled matplotlib extraction/drawing with exact final records.\\\",\n+    \\\"Require PDF and PNG exports from source for quantitative figures, PNG at 300 DPI, and use the PDF in LaTeX whenever available. Preserve vector diagram exports when available. Raster-only full-width output must be at least 2400 pixels wide; column/half-width raster-only output, if ever justified, must be at least 1200 pixels wide. A 5.5-inch 300-DPI preview is not sufficient for raster-only full-width placement; regenerate at the required source size, never upscale.\\\",\n+    \\\"The baseline table has five method rows, clear observation costs, MAE for all methods, and separately labeled selected-package RMSE/ranking if other statistics are not yet derived. Missing metrics are marked not reported, not inferred. Include the aggregate IRT paired interval, all principal reversals, lack of component attribution, metadata-limited ancestry, and fixed-snapshot uncertainty in main text, not only the supplement.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not add an algorithm-comparison ablation table: ablation_studies is empty. The optional nonlinear decoder retains a linear fallback, and candidate diagnostics are marked unverified. Code availability establishes the algorithm family, not that the nonlinear branch improved a particular benchmark. Component attribution and broad source-to-target transfer remain open questions, not completed experiments.\\\",\n+    \\\"The response-vector anchor and local IRT baselines are local implementations, not published-method leaderboard entries. Uniform and IRT share a uniform query path, whereas the proposed package also changes acquisition; paired errors compare packages at matching item budgets, not isolated decoders, matched training compute, or a globally optimal tuning budget.\\\",\n+    \\\"Before related-work prose, repair the relevance/readership gap in the supplied bibliography using only explicitly permitted direct-title sources from the task brief or focused unrelated foundational work. Current entries such as Derezinski2019BayesianED, Ravi2016ExperimentalDO and Uto2020AGM are possible contextual leads only, not proof of a new connection or a substitute for read task literature. Do not cite unrelated materials merely to reach a reference count, do not invent BibTeX keys, and do not claim metadata-only entries were read. This stage changes neither bibliography nor provenance and conducts no retrieval.\\\",\n+    \\\"Never identify, search for, infer, or follow citations toward the prohibited existing study. Use only permitted direct-source literature without citation-network expansion; if an accidental encounter occurs later, stop and document the location and reading extent. No such encounter was identified during this local-only framing stage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Anonymize ICLR submission text: omit authors, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, personal links and internal workspace URLs. Scientific limitations and precise LLM-use disclosure must survive all later review and revision. Do not claim a reviewer checklist was required when the supplied venue/style does not establish that requirement.\\\",\n+    \\\"This is a strategy-only deliverable: do not create paper.tex, claims_grounding.json, new experiments, figures, or final validation artifacts here. Check JSON shape, memo agreement, actual source-ID resolution, qualification preservation and layout/readability budgets only. Later authoritative analysis rankings route appendix material to Supplementary Information without retroactively rewriting this strategy.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Framing Strategy\n+\n+**Status:** ready for a bounded standalone study; relevant-literature repair is required before final related-work writing.  \n+**Prompt family:** \"'`paper_standalone` / `write-paper-standalone`.  \n+**Provisional title:** *Score-Targeted Subsets for Predicting LLM Benchmark Accuracy*.\n+\n+## Central Question and Thesis\n+\n+**Question.** How accurately can a source-trained, score-targeted shared item subset and decoder predict retained full-benchmark accuracy and model rankings at 5-, 10-, and 25-item budgets, relative to local benchmark-estimation baselines, and where does the comparison reverse?\n+\n+**Thesis.** On nine frozen benchmark matrices, the evaluated acquisition-and-decoding package has lower average accuracy-prediction error than the recorded baselines under equal benchmark, seed, and budget weighting. Its advantage over local IRT is not uniform across benchmarks. The measurements neither isolate an individual decoder component'\"'s benefit nor establish transfer beyond this snapshot.\n+\n+This is one estimation question with condition-specific evidence from leaderboard and HELM matrices, not two chronological experiments. Lead with the estimand, information constraints, and paired comparison, then explain where the average is misleading. A lower average error is the measured result; universal superiority and nonlinear-mechanism attribution are not.\n+\n+## Independent Evidence and Qualification Audit\n+\n+Read the final record independently of any campaign narrative. \"'`downstream_study` is absent. The authoritative qualification sources are:\n+\n+- `final.qualification.status`: `completed`.\n+- `final.qualification.outcome`: `qualified`.\n+- `final.qualification.correct`: `true`.\n+\n+These facts do not establish complete ancestry separation, contamination absence, out-of-snapshot validity, or any unreported gate diagnosis. Publication readiness is not scientific qualification. If a later authoritative record reports failed qualification, preserve that failure and its reported limitations throughout writing, review, audit, and revision; never infer its cause from retained scores. Missing diagnostics remain unknown.\n+\n+The final evidence contains three seeds, nine distinct cases, and budgets 5/10/25. A BBH normal replay is a determinism check, **not** an extra case or an independent measurement. The aggregate paired uncertainty object is repeated in each seed wrapper; use it once, not as three independent bootstrap results. Candidate-owned diagnostics are explicitly unverified.\n+\n+### Primary Numerical Anchors\n+\n+| Quantity | Recorded value | Grounding source |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Selected package MAE | 0.038991605535293065 | `final.metric.mae` |\n+| Selected package RMSE | 0.04837892636321264 | `final.metric.rmse` |\n+| Local IRT MAE | 0.05911223215296765 | `final.metric.irt_mae` |\n+| Uniform sampling MAE | 0.10520541810011626 | `final.metric.uniform_mae` |\n+| Source prior MAE | 0.08335016635136305 | `final.metric.prior_mae` |\n+| Response-vector anchor MAE | 0.15674229873896958 | `final.metric.anchor_mae` |\n+| Selected package Spearman | 0.8158480130897703 | `final.metric.spearman` |\n+| Selected package Kendall | 0.6715966634525837 | `final.metric.kendall` |\n+\n+All errors use score units in `[0,1]`; these are not 25-item-only results. The evaluator averages the declared budgets, seeds, and cases, with target-lineage-equal errors within cells. Ranking is computed from lineage-mean predictions and truths within each cell, not by pooling every model from different benchmarks. An average of cell RMSEs must not silently become a pooled RMSE.\n+\n+The recorded candidate-minus-IRT MAE is **-0.02012062661767458**, with recorded 95% interval **[-0.02570984836073398, -0.014632649205711504]**, grounded in `final.evidence.episodes`. Its 200-draw paired lineage-block bootstrap retains checkpoints and seeds within groups, averages cases equally, and conditions on the fixed cases. It is not uncertainty over new benchmarks, a component-ablation effect, or a generalization guarantee.\n+\n+The raw predictions also support direct case/budget views. Diagnostic postprocessing excluding replay and applying the evaluator'\"'s lineage weights finds candidate losses to local IRT on **math at all three budgets**, **legalbench at 5 and 25**, and **med_qa at 10 and 25**. Keep those cells visible in the main paper. Regenerate exact plot values from the raw records rather than quoting rounded framing diagnostics. Do not invent causes for the reversals or reuse the aggregate interval as a per-case interval.\n+\n+## Framing Decision and Alternatives\n+\n+**Decision: recentered.** This workspace has no resolved edit-context file, previous manuscript, \"'`aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` input. This is fresh framing; the label records a narrowing of the broad source-task brief, not an edit to an unseen paper. No inherited title or figure plan is authoritative.\n+\n+Compare the candidate framings explicitly:\n+\n+1. **Preserve a prior story with local updates:** no prior manuscript is supplied, and private memory is insufficient justification. Do not inherit a random-audit or discovery-order narrative.\n+2. **Broaden to a cross-setting method family:** the two data ecosystems support a common estimation question, but not an adaptive-per-target acquisition claim or a general transfer mechanism. Use condition-specific evidence under one thesis, not an enlarged capability claim.\n+3. **Recenter on the frozen final comparison:** strongest choice because it has paired baseline predictions, a defined scoring protocol, aggregate uncertainty, and scientifically informative reversals.\n+\n+Reject a random-audit unbiasedness paper: that earlier design is not the final evaluated package. Reject a nonlinear-decoder superiority paper: the selected source tree includes an incumbent fallback, its per-case branch selection is not attested, and no controlled ablation bundle exists. Reject a search-progress paper: the central question concerns prediction quality, not optimization dynamics.\n+\n+## Implementation and Staged-Input Impact\n+\n+Directly inspected local sources are under `results/ideas/03_log_odds_shift_residual_decoder/program_1/src/`: `program.py`, `surrogate.py`, and `nonlinear_decoder.py`, together with their implementation notes. The local selection manifest identifies this counterpart of the frozen selected package; no candidate was executed during framing.\n+\n+The core mechanism is source-weighted covariance between each item response and the full source score. Greedy acquisition maximizes squared conditional score covariance divided by regularized conditional item variance, using a nested common path and excluding already represented content groups. All-query ridge/offset decoding uses every legal queried answer. The implementation also offers a source-selected penalized log-odds shift, original-population score curve, and prefix-matched residual ridge, retaining the linear fallback. Explain these as the implemented decoder menu, not as independently validated contributions.\n+\n+`task/evaluate_final.py`, frozen manifests, and `task/resources/rebuild.py` establish the evaluator definitions and processed data scope. They support metadata-defined source/target lineage separation and conservative item reconciliation, not proof against undocumented derivatives, semantic duplicates, or pretraining contamination. The truth to be predicted is the full mean over **retained matrix columns**, not necessarily every original benchmark item.\n+\n+No existing figures or controlled ablations are available. Earlier implementations need not become main-paper narrative baggage. Their code may clarify design alternatives, but no final matched measurements support an original-program comparison. In particular, `task/program_0` is readable, but its old score from memory must not be imported. Keep the actual recorded comparators instead.\n+\n+## Narrow Method Set\n+\n+| Group | Role | Inclusion and boundary |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Score-targeted acquisition and source-selected score decoding | Proposed | Frozen final package; describe ridge/offset and optional nonlinear menu without asserting branch activation or component causality. |\n+| Uniform content-group sampling | Baseline | Group-representative sampling with group-mass correction and clipping; not silently ordinary unweighted averaging. |\n+| Source-score prior | Baseline | No target responses required; display observation cost as zero. |\n+| Response-vector anchors | Baseline | Local normalized-response/farthest-first representative selection and cluster-weighted score estimate; not an exact published-method reproduction. |\n+| Local Rasch-style IRT | Baseline | Strongest aggregate comparator; source-fitted item difficulty and queried target ability on the same uniform path as the sampling baseline. Not the full tinyBenchmarks system. |\n+\n+The measured comparison changes both acquisition and decoding at matching query budgets. It does not isolate either component, guarantee equal training compute, or establish that every comparator received globally optimal tuning.\n+\n+## Results Organization\n+\n+1. **Aggregate accuracy and paired uncertainty.** A compact five-method table gives absolute MAE, observation cost, and separately labeled RMSE/ranking where supported. The forest plot shows the four supplied paired MAE differences and intervals. No performance-success threshold or internal pipeline metric is needed.\n+2. **Benchmark-specific reversals.** Show all nine cases against IRT at each budget using signed differences with a common zero reference. Put the math, legalbench, and med_qa reversals in the main results and limitations, not only the supplement. Ecosystem panels are organizational, not evidence of a causal ecosystem effect.\n+3. **Ranking as a distinct objective.** Report the selected package'\"'s recorded Spearman and Kendall. Baseline rankings may be derived reproducibly from existing predictions using the evaluator's lineage-mean definition; if not derived, mark them “not reported,” never zero or inferred. Do not claim ranking superiority from selected-package values alone.\n+4. **Controls and evidence limits.** Permuted-source MAE is 0.06257521756337783 (\"'`final.metric.permuted_mae`); zero-response-control MAE is 0.21577661527598374 (`final.metric.constant_mae`). The constant intervention zeroes target observations; it is not necessarily a constant predictor. The source intervention independently circular-shifts each source row'\"'s columns. Describe sensitivity, not isolated ablation or validity proof. Duplicate histories and deterministic replay are protocol checks, not accuracy improvements.\n+\n+Development and final evaluations are separate. Development uses \"'`arc_challenge`, `ifeval`, `commonsense`, and `gsm`, seeds 101/211. Final uses `bbh`, `gpqa`, `mmlu_pro`, `musr`, `openllm_math`, `legalbench`, `math`, `med_qa`, and `mmlu`, seeds 1009/2003/3001. Do not compare their absolute averages as a paired improvement. There are no `study.*` sources here: no search-score differences, campaign win rates, or scored/unscored performance accounting is proposed. An unscored attempt would be missing evidence, never a measured loss.\n+\n+## Figure Plan and Physical Layout\n+\n+The inspected `paper.sty` sets **one 5.5-inch-wide text column and 9-inch text height**. This is not a two-column format: column width equals full text width. Use ordinary full-width figures, not `figure*`, 0.48-width defaults, or dense graphics rescued by shrinking. Render labels at least 9 points. None of the planned figures needs more than one panel per row.\n+\n+| Figure | Required design and evidence | Footprint and placement | Readability limits |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `score_prediction_overview` | One conceptual information-flow diagram: historical responses/full source scores → source-only shared subset design and decoder selection → legal target query answers → predicted full score; true retained target score remains beyond an external-scoring boundary. Mark nonlinear decoding optional/source-selected. Use `generate-concept-figure`. | Page 2, full 5.5-inch width; about 2.0-inch drawing height plus short caption, roughly 0.30 body page. Full width is necessary for legible matrix roles and information boundaries. | One panel, at most six blocks/categories, three visual information roles/series, at least 9-point labels. |\n+| `paired_error_comparison` | Horizontal forest plot of selected-minus-baseline MAE for uniform, prior, anchors, and IRT using the single supplied aggregate interval per comparator; common zero line. Generate with matplotlib. | Around page 6, full 5.5-inch width; about 1.7-inch axes height, roughly 0.26 body page with caption. Comparator labels, signed ticks, and intervals need the complete span. | One panel, four comparator categories, one series. Do not clip interval endpoints or duplicate the interval by seed. |\n+| `case_budget_reversals` | Two vertically stacked horizontal dot-plot panels: five leaderboard cases and four HELM cases. Each case has three offset budget symbols for candidate-minus-local-IRT MAE. Common signed x-axis; no connected progression lines. Generate with matplotlib. | Around page 7, full 5.5-inch width; about 3.2-inch total axes height, roughly 0.43 body page with caption. Stacking avoids illegible adjacent mini-panels and preserves all failure cells. | Two panels, one per row; at most five cases and three budget series per panel; shapes plus color, at least 9-point labels. |\n+\n+Only the overview uses the concept-figure workflow; the downstream orchestrator, not this framing stage, owns its execution. Preserve editable source and vector exports when available. Quantitative figures must have reproducible source and **both PDF and PNG exports**, with PNG at 300 DPI. LaTeX references the PDF whenever one exists. For raster-only full-width placement, regenerate at **at least 2400 pixels wide**; any justified narrower/column raster-only placement needs at least 1200 pixels. A 300-DPI preview at 5.5 inches is not enough for the raster-only full-width rule. Never upscale an existing image.\n+\n+## Body Budget and Scientific Structure\n+\n+Target about **8.5 body pages**, excluding references and substantive Supplementary Information:\n+\n+| Material | Body allocation including its floats |\n+| --- | ---: |\n+| Title, abstract, introduction, early overview | 1.5 pages |\n+| Problem/estimand and focused related work | 1.0 page |\n+| Weighted acquisition, decoding, source-only tuning | 1.8 pages |\n+| Frozen data, fair protocol, baseline definitions | 1.1 pages |\n+| Aggregate uncertainty, ranking, case/budget reversals | 2.0 pages |\n+| Interpretation, limitations, conclusion | 1.1 pages |\n+\n+Suggested headings: **Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Score-Targeted Subset Prediction; Evaluation Protocol; Results** with subsections **Aggregate Accuracy and Conditional Uncertainty** and **Benchmark-Specific Reversals and Ranking; Scope and Limitations; Conclusion**.\n+\n+Spend available space on precise estimands, the acquisition/decoder equations, group weighting, fold-local refitting, baseline definitions, interpretation of failures, and uncertainty assumptions. Do not add unsupported ablations, inflated related work, repeated plots, or oversized graphics to fill pages. The venue requires 8–9 body pages; an eight-page body must have its final page at least 75% full, and a nine-page body must not overflow the body limit. Check final layout later, not by final-paper validation during framing.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+**Purpose:** add reproducibility and complete evidence disaggregation without hiding any essential result, reversal, or limitation. Later authoritative appendix rankings can add material here without retroactively changing this strategy.\n+\n+1. **Weighted Acquisition and Decoder Specification.** Full weighted covariance/conditional-gain and decoder equations, source-only tuning shortlists and group partitions, optional branch, clipping, and zero-budget/insufficient-group fallbacks. Ground in the inspected selected source tree linked to `final.evidence.episodes` and `final.qualification.status`. Clearly distinguish specification from ablation evidence.\n+2. **Frozen Data and Lineage/Content Provenance.** Pinned snapshot, rebuild script, retained columns, actual evaluated dimensions, grouping rules, hashes, and conservative ancestry/content limitations. Ground the evaluated data link in `final.evidence.episodes` and detail provenance from the local manifests. Do not substitute generic task-brief model counts.\n+3. **Complete Benchmark, Budget, and Seed Results.** Every non-replay normal cell and its four baseline prediction arrays; reproducible MAE/ranking extraction and reconciliation to the recorded final metrics. Newly derived baseline statistics are postprocessing, not new runs; no invented cell intervals. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.mae`, `final.metric.rmse`, `final.metric.spearman`, `final.metric.kendall`, and the four baseline `final.metric.*` entries.\n+4. **Paired Uncertainty and Observation Controls.** The single fixed-case bootstrap, checkpoint/seed retention, equal-case weights, evaluator missing-cell policy, recorded zero failed normal cells, and intervention/replay/duplicate-history definitions. A no-failure count is not a performance-success rate or universal validity certificate. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.constant_mae`, `final.metric.permuted_mae`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.status`.\n+5. **Reproduction and Evidence Boundaries.** Anonymized reconstruction/evaluation commands based on existing scripts and dependency/specification files, seeds/budgets, hashes, and an eventual script-to-table/figure mapping. Label unrerun commands truthfully, report CPU requirements as requirements, and give no unmeasured speedup or end-to-end time. Include the absence of component ablations/branch-selection diagnostics. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes` and all three `final.qualification.*` entries.\n+6. **LLM Usage.** The separately required venue section: precise documented roles in ideation, implementation, citation-query planning, framing, and eventual writing/figure assistance; distinguish evaluator measurements from agent-produced interpretation. Disclose actual verification, not fictitious human review. Framing used local inspection and existing-prediction postprocessing, not candidate execution. Link measurements to `final.evidence.episodes`; process roles come from the supplied task/memory provenance, which is not quantitative evidence.\n+\n+## Literature and Readiness Boundary\n+\n+The supplied bibliography is mostly off-topic. The retrieval log shows its quota was exhausted before the planned task-specific title queries; relevant source metadata does not imply source reading. Some existing foundational entries may be useful leads, such as `Derezinski2019BayesianED`, `Ravi2016ExperimentalDO`, and `Uto2020AGM`, but their exact relevance must be checked and they do not substitute for the permitted benchmark-prediction literature.\n+\n+Before final related-work writing, repair this gap using permitted direct-title sources from the task brief and focused unrelated foundational material, maintain citation provenance, and cite only genuinely consulted relevant works with actual BibTeX keys. Do not cite tangential engineering papers to reach a target count. This is a **citation-readiness prerequisite**, not a reason to invent a weaker or broader empirical story. This stage does not modify references or perform retrieval.\n+\n+Never infer or search for the prohibited paper'\"'s identity or expand citation networks toward it. If a later accidental encounter occurs, stop and document location and reading extent. This local-only framing stage identified no such encounter. Omit authors, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, personal links and internal URLs from the anonymous manuscript. Do not invent a venue checklist requirement absent supporting venue instructions.\n+\n+## Anti-Diary and Overclaim Guardrails\n+\n+Avoid headings **Search Progression; Campaign Phases; Milestones; First Valid Result; Iteration History; Experiment A / Experiment B; From Audit to Ridge to Nonlinear; Winning Configuration; Nonlinear Decoder Ablation; Universal Benchmark Prediction**.\n+\n+Avoid wording **we then tried; subsequent improvements; first valid result; next-best; later variants; state of the art; wins on every benchmark; proves generalization; leakage-free; the nonlinear component caused the gain; unbiased rankings; adaptive per-target acquisition**. Internal field names and pipeline labels listed in the JSON forbidden phrases are private bookkeeping, never visible metrics or prose recommendations.\n+\n+Do not conflate source-only fitting with complete validity; score error with ranking preservation; aggregate confidence with new-benchmark uncertainty; local baseline families with exact published systems; or an implemented optional module with a measured component gain. Anonymization, qualification facts, mixed results, and scientific limitations must survive later writing, review, audit, and revision.\n+\n+## Stage Boundary\n+\n+Deliver only \"'`paper_strategy.json` and this mirrored memo, with append-only memory updates. Do not create `paper.tex`, `claims_grounding.json`, figures, new experiments, or final-paper validation outputs. Validate strategy schema, source-ID existence, figure budgets, qualification preservation, and memo agreement only. No final paper has been drafted in this stage.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$(cat)\"; }\napply_patch <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Score-Targeted Subsets for Predicting LLM Benchmark Accuracy\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"How accurately can a source-trained, score-targeted shared item subset and decoder predict retained full-benchmark accuracy and model rankings at 5-, 10-, and 25-item budgets, relative to local benchmark-estimation baselines, and where does the comparison reverse?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On nine frozen benchmark matrices, the evaluated score-targeted acquisition-and-decoding package has lower average accuracy-prediction error than the recorded baselines when averaging equally over benchmarks, seeds, and query budgets, but its advantage over local IRT is not uniform across benchmarks and does not establish the benefit of any individual decoder component or transfer beyond this snapshot.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation of one frozen package against paired, budget-matched local estimators, including an evaluator-provided lineage-block uncertainty analysis. The independent qualification sources report completed and qualified; no downstream_study is present. Aggregate candidate MAE is 0.038991605535293065, compared with local IRT 0.05911223215296765 and uniform sampling 0.10520541810011626. The IRT paired MAE-difference interval excludes zero conditional on the fixed cases, while the raw case-by-budget predictions reveal reversals in math, legalbench, and med_qa. These reversals are part of the thesis, not inconvenient supplementary-only results. Prefer one shared estimation question with condition-specific evidence blocks for the leaderboard and HELM matrices, not separate chronological experiments. Reject a random-audit unbiasedness paper because that is not the final evaluated package; reject a nonlinear-decoder superiority paper because activation and isolated component effects are unverified; reject a universal or adaptive-evaluation story because the evaluated item path is source-only and shared across targets. The empirical framing is ready, but the supplied bibliography needs task-relevant, permitted-source repair before a defensible final related-work section can be written.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"This is fresh framing, not an enabled manuscript-edit pass: no resolved edit-context file, previous_paper manuscript, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory is supplied here. The recentered label describes narrowing the broad source-task brief to the frozen evaluated package and its heterogeneous accuracy, not a claim to have revised an unseen prior manuscript. Preserve-only framing has no prior text to justify; broadening to a shared adaptive or cross-setting method family is unsupported; recentering on the final paired evidence is strongest. Do not inherit a title or figure plan from private memory.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation, read independently of the absent downstream_study, supplies nine distinct final cases, three seeds, three query budgets, paired baseline predictions, and qualification facts. It changes the center of gravity from broad method search to a frozen-package comparison.\\\",\n+    \\\"Direct inspection of results/ideas/03_log_odds_shift_residual_decoder/program_1/src/program.py, surrogate.py, and nonlinear_decoder.py establishes a common score-covariance item path, all-query ridge/offset decoding, and a source-selected optional log-odds/residual branch with an incumbent fallback. The source tree is the local counterpart identified by the frozen selection manifest; no candidate was executed in this stage. No per-case selected branch is attested by the final evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"task/evaluate_final.py and task/resources/final/*_manifest.json clarify group-weighted errors, lineage-mean ranking, equal-case aggregation, replay exclusion, local baseline definitions, content reconciliation, and metadata-limited lineage separation. They prevent claims about universally independent models or every original benchmark item.\\\",\n+    \\\"Diagnostic postprocessing of final raw predictions, excluding replay and using lineage-equal weights, identifies local IRT reversals: math at all budgets, legalbench at 5 and 25, and med_qa at 10 and 25. These derived diagnostic signs determine the main figure plan; exact plotted values must be regenerated from the same records, not copied from rounded diagnostics.\\\",\n+    \\\"No ablation studies or previously generated figures are supplied. The earlier estimator implementations are development-only context, not mandatory main-paper groups or controlled component ablations. No new experiments are prerequisites for this bounded comparison story.\\\",\n+    \\\"VENUE.md and paper.sty require an anonymized ICLR 2026 single-column paper with 5.5-inch text width, 9-inch text height, and an 8-to-9-page body. The figure plan therefore uses full-text-width placement, not two-column assumptions.\\\",\n+    \\\"references.bib and references_provenance.json contain mostly off-topic retrievals; reference_retrieval.log shows the quota was exhausted before the planned LLM-specific title queries. Existing metadata is not evidence that relevant literature was read. No retrieval, citation-network browsing, or prohibited-literature identification was attempted during framing.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Score-targeted acquisition and source-selected score decoding\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"This is the frozen final package: lineage-weighted source response/score covariance, regularized conditional-gain selection with one representative per content group, a nested common subset, and all-observation decoding. Explain linear ridge/offset and optional log-odds plus residual ridge as implemented alternatives within the package; do not claim the optional branch was active or responsible for the measured gain.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Uniform content-group sampling\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Recorded, budget-matched simple comparator. The local implementation samples distinct content-group representatives, accounts for group mass, and clips its estimate; describe this rather than silently substituting an ordinary unweighted item mean.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Source-score prior\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Recorded no-target-response reference quantifies what can be predicted from source scores alone; its observation cost is zero even when displayed beside the other methods at each budget.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Response-vector anchors\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Recorded source-response representative selection and cluster-weighted averaging contextualize a structurally different acquisition/estimation family. The local normalized-response, farthest-first implementation is not an attested reproduction of the published Anchor Points method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Local Rasch-style IRT estimator\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The strongest recorded aggregate comparator and the essential reference for heterogeneous failures. It uses source-fitted item difficulty, the same uniform query path as the uniform baseline, and queried-response target-ability fitting. It is not the complete tinyBenchmarks system or an exhaustive tuned IRT comparison.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary estimand: full mean binary accuracy over the retained, reconciled item matrix, not necessarily the original unfiltered benchmark. Primary error is target-lineage-equal MAE, then equally averaged across the declared budgets, seeds, and nine cases. Source and target model-lineage group assignments are disjoint under the supplied metadata policy, not under a proved complete ancestry relation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main aggregate table: selected package MAE 0.038991605535293065 and RMSE 0.04837892636321264; local IRT MAE 0.05911223215296765; uniform 0.10520541810011626; source prior 0.08335016635136305; anchors 0.15674229873896958. Ground every reported final metric in final.metric.* and keep raw score units in [0,1]. Do not imply these averages are specifically 25-item results.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main paired uncertainty view: candidate-minus-IRT MAE -0.02012062661767458, recorded 95% interval [-0.02570984836073398, -0.014632649205711504]. Also show the recorded paired differences and intervals against uniform, prior, and anchors. The 200-draw lineage-block bootstrap retains seeds and budgets within groups and conditions on the fixed nine cases; the identical interval repeated in each seed wrapper is one aggregate analysis, not three independent intervals.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main heterogeneity view: all nine cases at each budget, expressed as paired candidate-minus-local-IRT MAE with a common zero reference. Preserve math losses at every budget, legalbench reversals at 5 and 25, and med_qa reversals at 10 and 25. Do not infer causes from ecosystem membership, source count, or benchmark names. Any case-specific interval would require a documented new postprocessing analysis; the supplied aggregate interval cannot be reused as a per-case interval.\\\",\n+    \\\"Ranking is a distinct outcome, not an inferred consequence of MAE: final Spearman 0.8158480130897703 and Kendall 0.6715966634525837 are calculated on lineage-mean predictions/truth and then averaged by the evaluator. Do not concatenate models from different benchmarks into one correlation. Baseline ranking cells may be filled only by a reproducible extraction from existing baseline predictions with exactly the same rules; otherwise show not reported, not zero, and make no ranking-superiority claim.\\\",\n+    \\\"Robustness/control reporting: recorded permuted-source MAE 0.06257521756337783 and zero-response-control MAE 0.21577661527598374 concern interventions on the same package. Constant refers to zeroed target observations in the protocol, not necessarily a constant predictor; permuted refers to independent row-wise circular shifts of source columns. These are sensitivity checks, not isolated ablations or proof of the mechanism, validity, or absence of contamination.\\\",\n+    \\\"Search and final are different evidence scopes: development uses arc_challenge, ifeval, commonsense, and gsm with seeds 101 and 211; final uses bbh, gpqa, mmlu_pro, musr, openllm_math, legalbench, math, med_qa, and mmlu with seeds 1009, 2003, and 3001. No pooled search/final table, before/after gain, cross-variant significance, search-score delta, or attempt-loss rate is planned. No study.* namespace exists here to support a downstream campaign accounting analysis.\\\",\n+    \\\"Preserve original-comparator honesty: the initial anchor/ridge implementation is readable under task/program_0 but has no matched final measurements in this bundle; omit a quantitative original-program comparison rather than borrowing an incumbent score from memory. Retain the four actual recorded final comparators. No controlled ablation bundle exists.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: historical source responses and full source scores produce one common score-targeted item path; a new target contributes only queried answers to a source-selected decoder; complete retained target scores are used solely for external evaluation. Distinguish source fitting, legal target observation, and scoring by labeled lanes and a visual information boundary. Mark optional nonlinear decoding as source-selected, not as an experimentally established mechanism.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, aggregate paired comparison: a horizontal forest plot of candidate-minus-baseline MAE for the four recorded baselines, using the one supplied aggregate lineage-block interval per comparator and a zero line. A nearby compact table carries absolute errors and separately identified ranking results.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, scope and reversals: two vertically stacked dot-plot panels, one with the five leaderboard cases and one with the four HELM cases; within each case show the three budget-specific candidate-minus-local-IRT MAEs using displaced symbols, not connected progression curves. A common signed x-axis exposes local losses as well as gains.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"score_prediction_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the estimation target, shared score-directed subset, source-selected decoder, and target-truth information boundary legible at a glance.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"information_role\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none_conceptual_information_flow\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"none\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected paper.sty sets one 5.5-inch-wide column and 9-inch text height. Use the full 5.5-inch text width, about 2.0 inches of drawing height plus a short caption, early on page 2; a half-width figure would make matrix labels and the training/evaluation boundary too small. Allocate about 0.30 body page including caption. Use one panel, at most six labeled blocks, and at least 9-point rendered labels.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"paired_error_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show the signed aggregate error difference and conditional uncertainty against every recorded baseline without equating average gains with universal wins.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"forest_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"baseline_method\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"candidate_minus_baseline_mae_with_recorded_95_percent_interval\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"none_equal_case_budget_seed_aggregate\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use the single-column 5.5-inch text width and about 1.7 inches of axes height, with four comparator rows and one point/interval per row. The full span preserves readable comparator names, signed ticks, and a zero reference at 9-point or larger type. Place near the aggregate results, around page 6; budget about 0.26 body page including caption. Do not squeeze it into a hypothetical two-column slot or truncate interval endpoints.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 1\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"case_budget_reversals\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose budget-specific benchmark heterogeneity, including where the selected package loses to the strongest recorded aggregate baseline.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"faceted_horizontal_dot_plot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"benchmark\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"candidate_minus_local_irt_mae\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"data_ecosystem_with_budget_symbols\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"At the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width, stack the five-case and four-case panels vertically in one column rather than shrinking nine case labels into adjacent mini-panels. Target about 3.2 inches total axes height, one shared signed x-scale, three offset symbols per case for 5/10/25 items, and labels at least 9 points. Place around page 7 and budget about 0.43 body page including caption. Use labels or shapes as well as color; never suppress positive differences or connect points as a search trajectory.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 5,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Supply reimplementation, auditability, and complete evidence disaggregation after the references while keeping aggregate uncertainty, benchmark reversals, and the principal limitations in the main paper; no proposed experiment is presented as completed.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Weighted Acquisition and Decoder Specification\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand the weighted covariance definitions, conditional squared score-covariance over regularized conditional item variance, content-group exclusion, ridge/offset prediction, and optional penalized log-odds/full-population curve/residual-ridge equations. Transcribe the implemented tuning shortlists, fold construction, clipping, zero-budget fallback, and insufficient-group/allowance fallback from the inspected selected src/surrogate.py and src/nonlinear_decoder.py. Treat component behavior as code specification, not measured ablation evidence. The final evidence and frozen tree metadata link this specification to the studied package.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Frozen Data and Lineage/Content Provenance\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the pinned benchmark-prediction snapshot, task/resources/rebuild.py, retained columns, source/target row and item-group policies, and file hashes in task/resources/final/*_manifest.json. Reconcile dimensions with the evaluated arrays rather than generic counts from the task brief. Include metadata-limited ancestry and conservative common-stem limitations; these also receive a concise main-text disclosure. Do not expose model identities or file paths as a substitute for scientific grouping definitions.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Benchmark, Budget, and Seed Results\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate every non-replay normal case/budget/seed result from final raw predictions for the selected package and four recorded baseline prediction arrays. Compute lineage-equal MAE and the evaluator-defined ranking summaries reproducibly, reconcile the primary aggregates to final.metric.*, and retain all loss cells. Identify any newly derived baseline RMSE or ranking statistics as postprocessing of existing predictions, not new experimental runs. Do not invent intervals for individual cells.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.rmse\\\", \\\"final.metric.spearman\\\", \\\"final.metric.kendall\\\", \\\"final.metric.irt_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.uniform_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.anchor_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.prior_mae\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Paired Uncertainty and Observation Controls\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Explain the single recorded 200-draw, fixed-case, lineage-block bootstrap, retention of checkpoints/seeds within groups, equal-case averaging, and treatment of missing cells in the evaluator policy. Report the actual recorded zero failed normal cells, without converting it into a performance success rate. Expand normal, zeroed-target-observation, source-column-shift, duplicate-history, and deterministic-replay definitions from task/evaluate_final.py. Keep control behavior distinct from full validity certification and do not count the BBH replay as another benchmark.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.constant_mae\\\", \\\"final.metric.permuted_mae\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Reproduction and Evidence Boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Provide anonymized data reconstruction and evaluation commands based on the inspected scripts, available requirement/specification files, artifact hashes, exact recorded seeds and budgets, and a table mapping each final table/figure to its eventual extraction script and source records. Commands not rerun by the writer must be labeled as such. Describe CPU requirements as requirements, not measured speedups; give no unmeasured end-to-end runtime. Preserve final completed/qualified outcome separately from search feedback, and record the absence of controlled ablations and per-case decoder-selection diagnostics.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented use of LLM agents for research ideation, candidate implementation, reference-query planning, paper framing, and eventual writing/figure assistance, distinguishing these roles from evaluator-produced measurements. Identify verification actually performed rather than inventing human review. Document that framing performed local artifact inspection and prediction postprocessing only, not candidate execution or additional experiments. Track any later literature incident truthfully without guessing the prohibited work's identity.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Iteration History\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"From Audit to Ridge to Nonlinear\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Configuration\\\",\n+    \\\"Nonlinear Decoder Ablation\\\",\n+    \\\"Universal Benchmark Prediction\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\",\n+    \\\"wins on every benchmark\\\",\n+    \\\"proves generalization\\\",\n+    \\\"leakage-free\\\",\n+    \\\"the nonlinear component caused the gain\\\",\n+    \\\"unbiased rankings\\\",\n+    \\\"adaptive per-target acquisition\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Plan an approximately 8.5-page ICLR 2026 body including figures/tables, excluding references and substantive Supplementary Information. Allocate 1.5 pages to title/abstract/introduction plus the early overview; 1.0 to problem/estimand and focused related work; 1.8 to acquisition, decoding and source-only tuning; 1.1 to frozen protocol/data/baseline definitions; 2.0 to aggregate uncertainty, ranking and case/budget reversals; and 1.1 to limitations, interpretation and conclusion. If the body ends at eight pages, the final body page must be at least 75% full; never exceed nine body pages. Use available space for equations, definitions and evidence interpretation, not padding or a run diary.\\\",\n+    \\\"Suggested thesis-first headings: Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Score-Targeted Subset Prediction; Evaluation Protocol; Aggregate Accuracy and Conditional Uncertainty; Benchmark-Specific Reversals and Ranking; Scope and Limitations; Conclusion. Results subsections may share one top-level Results heading. Put substantive Supplementary Information after references; include a separate LLM Usage section there.\\\",\n+    \\\"Qualification is independently grounded in final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, and final.qualification.correct=true. Do not derive qualification from a search score, remembered acceptance statement, or publication readiness. Do not claim unseen gate diagnostics establish adaptivity, generalization, or complete validity. If a later authoritative evaluation changes the outcome, preserve that outcome and any reported limitations throughout writing, review, audit, and revision; missing causes stay unknown.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use final.metric.* for final numbers and final.evidence.episodes for paired analyses. There are no study.* sources and no downstream_study; omit search-score differences and scored/unscored accounting rather than reconstructing them from private memory. Never treat an unscored attempt as a measured loss. Report no inherited original-program metric without matched evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only artifact identifiers, hashes, result.* search fields, and internal selection labels belong in evidence bookkeeping, not titles, abstract, tables, or visible metrics. Refer to the frozen package, model variants, query budgets, and recorded evaluation. Source identifiers listed in this strategy are audit anchors, not literal paper prose.\\\",\n+    \\\"All figure spans refer to the actual one-column 5.5-inch text width in paper.sty: column width and full text width coincide here. Do not use figure* or 0.48-width two-column defaults. Respect the per-figure height, label and panel budgets; at most two total panels are needed and no figure has more than one panel per row. Prefer a page-2 overview to adding a dense late appendix architecture diagram.\\\",\n+    \\\"Only score_prediction_overview uses generate-concept-figure; the downstream orchestrator owns that pipeline, and this stage only plans it. Require an editable diagram source and deterministic faithful export; do not fabricate illustrative outcome values or imply active nonlinear decoding. Quantitative figures use source-controlled matplotlib extraction/drawing with exact final records.\\\",\n+    \\\"Require PDF and PNG exports from source for quantitative figures, PNG at 300 DPI, and use the PDF in LaTeX whenever available. Preserve vector diagram exports when available. Raster-only full-width output must be at least 2400 pixels wide; column/half-width raster-only output, if ever justified, must be at least 1200 pixels wide. A 5.5-inch 300-DPI preview is not sufficient for raster-only full-width placement; regenerate at the required source size, never upscale.\\\",\n+    \\\"The baseline table has five method rows, clear observation costs, MAE for all methods, and separately labeled selected-package RMSE/ranking if other statistics are not yet derived. Missing metrics are marked not reported, not inferred. Include the aggregate IRT paired interval, all principal reversals, lack of component attribution, metadata-limited ancestry, and fixed-snapshot uncertainty in main text, not only the supplement.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not add an algorithm-comparison ablation table: ablation_studies is empty. The optional nonlinear decoder retains a linear fallback, and candidate diagnostics are marked unverified. Code availability establishes the algorithm family, not that the nonlinear branch improved a particular benchmark. Component attribution and broad source-to-target transfer remain open questions, not completed experiments.\\\",\n+    \\\"The response-vector anchor and local IRT baselines are local implementations, not published-method leaderboard entries. Uniform and IRT share a uniform query path, whereas the proposed package also changes acquisition; paired errors compare packages at matching item budgets, not isolated decoders, matched training compute, or a globally optimal tuning budget.\\\",\n+    \\\"Before related-work prose, repair the relevance/readership gap in the supplied bibliography using only explicitly permitted direct-title sources from the task brief or focused unrelated foundational work. Current entries such as Derezinski2019BayesianED, Ravi2016ExperimentalDO and Uto2020AGM are possible contextual leads only, not proof of a new connection or a substitute for read task literature. Do not cite unrelated materials merely to reach a reference count, do not invent BibTeX keys, and do not claim metadata-only entries were read. This stage changes neither bibliography nor provenance and conducts no retrieval.\\\",\n+    \\\"Never identify, search for, infer, or follow citations toward the prohibited existing study. Use only permitted direct-source literature without citation-network expansion; if an accidental encounter occurs later, stop and document the location and reading extent. No such encounter was identified during this local-only framing stage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Anonymize ICLR submission text: omit authors, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, personal links and internal workspace URLs. Scientific limitations and precise LLM-use disclosure must survive all later review and revision. Do not claim a reviewer checklist was required when the supplied venue/style does not establish that requirement.\\\",\n+    \\\"This is a strategy-only deliverable: do not create paper.tex, claims_grounding.json, new experiments, figures, or final validation artifacts here. Check JSON shape, memo agreement, actual source-ID resolution, qualification preservation and layout/readability budgets only. Later authoritative analysis rankings route appendix material to Supplementary Information without retroactively rewriting this strategy.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Framing Strategy\n+\n+**Status:** ready for a bounded standalone study; relevant-literature repair is required before final related-work writing.  \n+**Prompt family:** \"'`paper_standalone` / `write-paper-standalone`.  \n+**Provisional title:** *Score-Targeted Subsets for Predicting LLM Benchmark Accuracy*.\n+\n+## Central Question and Thesis\n+\n+**Question.** How accurately can a source-trained, score-targeted shared item subset and decoder predict retained full-benchmark accuracy and model rankings at 5-, 10-, and 25-item budgets, relative to local benchmark-estimation baselines, and where does the comparison reverse?\n+\n+**Thesis.** On nine frozen benchmark matrices, the evaluated acquisition-and-decoding package has lower average accuracy-prediction error than the recorded baselines under equal benchmark, seed, and budget weighting. Its advantage over local IRT is not uniform across benchmarks. The measurements neither isolate an individual decoder component'\"'s benefit nor establish transfer beyond this snapshot.\n+\n+This is one estimation question with condition-specific evidence from leaderboard and HELM matrices, not two chronological experiments. Lead with the estimand, information constraints, and paired comparison, then explain where the average is misleading. A lower average error is the measured result; universal superiority and nonlinear-mechanism attribution are not.\n+\n+## Independent Evidence and Qualification Audit\n+\n+Read the final record independently of any campaign narrative. \"'`downstream_study` is absent. The authoritative qualification sources are:\n+\n+- `final.qualification.status`: `completed`.\n+- `final.qualification.outcome`: `qualified`.\n+- `final.qualification.correct`: `true`.\n+\n+These facts do not establish complete ancestry separation, contamination absence, out-of-snapshot validity, or any unreported gate diagnosis. Publication readiness is not scientific qualification. If a later authoritative record reports failed qualification, preserve that failure and its reported limitations throughout writing, review, audit, and revision; never infer its cause from retained scores. Missing diagnostics remain unknown.\n+\n+The final evidence contains three seeds, nine distinct cases, and budgets 5/10/25. A BBH normal replay is a determinism check, **not** an extra case or an independent measurement. The aggregate paired uncertainty object is repeated in each seed wrapper; use it once, not as three independent bootstrap results. Candidate-owned diagnostics are explicitly unverified.\n+\n+### Primary Numerical Anchors\n+\n+| Quantity | Recorded value | Grounding source |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Selected package MAE | 0.038991605535293065 | `final.metric.mae` |\n+| Selected package RMSE | 0.04837892636321264 | `final.metric.rmse` |\n+| Local IRT MAE | 0.05911223215296765 | `final.metric.irt_mae` |\n+| Uniform sampling MAE | 0.10520541810011626 | `final.metric.uniform_mae` |\n+| Source prior MAE | 0.08335016635136305 | `final.metric.prior_mae` |\n+| Response-vector anchor MAE | 0.15674229873896958 | `final.metric.anchor_mae` |\n+| Selected package Spearman | 0.8158480130897703 | `final.metric.spearman` |\n+| Selected package Kendall | 0.6715966634525837 | `final.metric.kendall` |\n+\n+All errors use score units in `[0,1]`; these are not 25-item-only results. The evaluator averages the declared budgets, seeds, and cases, with target-lineage-equal errors within cells. Ranking is computed from lineage-mean predictions and truths within each cell, not by pooling every model from different benchmarks. An average of cell RMSEs must not silently become a pooled RMSE.\n+\n+The recorded candidate-minus-IRT MAE is **-0.02012062661767458**, with recorded 95% interval **[-0.02570984836073398, -0.014632649205711504]**, grounded in `final.evidence.episodes`. Its 200-draw paired lineage-block bootstrap retains checkpoints and seeds within groups, averages cases equally, and conditions on the fixed cases. It is not uncertainty over new benchmarks, a component-ablation effect, or a generalization guarantee.\n+\n+The raw predictions also support direct case/budget views. Diagnostic postprocessing excluding replay and applying the evaluator'\"'s lineage weights finds candidate losses to local IRT on **math at all three budgets**, **legalbench at 5 and 25**, and **med_qa at 10 and 25**. Keep those cells visible in the main paper. Regenerate exact plot values from the raw records rather than quoting rounded framing diagnostics. Do not invent causes for the reversals or reuse the aggregate interval as a per-case interval.\n+\n+## Framing Decision and Alternatives\n+\n+**Decision: recentered.** This workspace has no resolved edit-context file, previous manuscript, \"'`aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` input. This is fresh framing; the label records a narrowing of the broad source-task brief, not an edit to an unseen paper. No inherited title or figure plan is authoritative.\n+\n+Compare the candidate framings explicitly:\n+\n+1. **Preserve a prior story with local updates:** no prior manuscript is supplied, and private memory is insufficient justification. Do not inherit a random-audit or discovery-order narrative.\n+2. **Broaden to a cross-setting method family:** the two data ecosystems support a common estimation question, but not an adaptive-per-target acquisition claim or a general transfer mechanism. Use condition-specific evidence under one thesis, not an enlarged capability claim.\n+3. **Recenter on the frozen final comparison:** strongest choice because it has paired baseline predictions, a defined scoring protocol, aggregate uncertainty, and scientifically informative reversals.\n+\n+Reject a random-audit unbiasedness paper: that earlier design is not the final evaluated package. Reject a nonlinear-decoder superiority paper: the selected source tree includes an incumbent fallback, its per-case branch selection is not attested, and no controlled ablation bundle exists. Reject a search-progress paper: the central question concerns prediction quality, not optimization dynamics.\n+\n+## Implementation and Staged-Input Impact\n+\n+Directly inspected local sources are under `results/ideas/03_log_odds_shift_residual_decoder/program_1/src/`: `program.py`, `surrogate.py`, and `nonlinear_decoder.py`, together with their implementation notes. The local selection manifest identifies this counterpart of the frozen selected package; no candidate was executed during framing.\n+\n+The core mechanism is source-weighted covariance between each item response and the full source score. Greedy acquisition maximizes squared conditional score covariance divided by regularized conditional item variance, using a nested common path and excluding already represented content groups. All-query ridge/offset decoding uses every legal queried answer. The implementation also offers a source-selected penalized log-odds shift, original-population score curve, and prefix-matched residual ridge, retaining the linear fallback. Explain these as the implemented decoder menu, not as independently validated contributions.\n+\n+`task/evaluate_final.py`, frozen manifests, and `task/resources/rebuild.py` establish the evaluator definitions and processed data scope. They support metadata-defined source/target lineage separation and conservative item reconciliation, not proof against undocumented derivatives, semantic duplicates, or pretraining contamination. The truth to be predicted is the full mean over **retained matrix columns**, not necessarily every original benchmark item.\n+\n+No existing figures or controlled ablations are available. Earlier implementations need not become main-paper narrative baggage. Their code may clarify design alternatives, but no final matched measurements support an original-program comparison. In particular, `task/program_0` is readable, but its old score from memory must not be imported. Keep the actual recorded comparators instead.\n+\n+## Narrow Method Set\n+\n+| Group | Role | Inclusion and boundary |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Score-targeted acquisition and source-selected score decoding | Proposed | Frozen final package; describe ridge/offset and optional nonlinear menu without asserting branch activation or component causality. |\n+| Uniform content-group sampling | Baseline | Group-representative sampling with group-mass correction and clipping; not silently ordinary unweighted averaging. |\n+| Source-score prior | Baseline | No target responses required; display observation cost as zero. |\n+| Response-vector anchors | Baseline | Local normalized-response/farthest-first representative selection and cluster-weighted score estimate; not an exact published-method reproduction. |\n+| Local Rasch-style IRT | Baseline | Strongest aggregate comparator; source-fitted item difficulty and queried target ability on the same uniform path as the sampling baseline. Not the full tinyBenchmarks system. |\n+\n+The measured comparison changes both acquisition and decoding at matching query budgets. It does not isolate either component, guarantee equal training compute, or establish that every comparator received globally optimal tuning.\n+\n+## Results Organization\n+\n+1. **Aggregate accuracy and paired uncertainty.** A compact five-method table gives absolute MAE, observation cost, and separately labeled RMSE/ranking where supported. The forest plot shows the four supplied paired MAE differences and intervals. No performance-success threshold or internal pipeline metric is needed.\n+2. **Benchmark-specific reversals.** Show all nine cases against IRT at each budget using signed differences with a common zero reference. Put the math, legalbench, and med_qa reversals in the main results and limitations, not only the supplement. Ecosystem panels are organizational, not evidence of a causal ecosystem effect.\n+3. **Ranking as a distinct objective.** Report the selected package'\"'s recorded Spearman and Kendall. Baseline rankings may be derived reproducibly from existing predictions using the evaluator's lineage-mean definition; if not derived, mark them “not reported,” never zero or inferred. Do not claim ranking superiority from selected-package values alone.\n+4. **Controls and evidence limits.** Permuted-source MAE is 0.06257521756337783 (\"'`final.metric.permuted_mae`); zero-response-control MAE is 0.21577661527598374 (`final.metric.constant_mae`). The constant intervention zeroes target observations; it is not necessarily a constant predictor. The source intervention independently circular-shifts each source row'\"'s columns. Describe sensitivity, not isolated ablation or validity proof. Duplicate histories and deterministic replay are protocol checks, not accuracy improvements.\n+\n+Development and final evaluations are separate. Development uses \"'`arc_challenge`, `ifeval`, `commonsense`, and `gsm`, seeds 101/211. Final uses `bbh`, `gpqa`, `mmlu_pro`, `musr`, `openllm_math`, `legalbench`, `math`, `med_qa`, and `mmlu`, seeds 1009/2003/3001. Do not compare their absolute averages as a paired improvement. There are no `study.*` sources here: no search-score differences, campaign win rates, or scored/unscored performance accounting is proposed. An unscored attempt would be missing evidence, never a measured loss.\n+\n+## Figure Plan and Physical Layout\n+\n+The inspected `paper.sty` sets **one 5.5-inch-wide text column and 9-inch text height**. This is not a two-column format: column width equals full text width. Use ordinary full-width figures, not `figure*`, 0.48-width defaults, or dense graphics rescued by shrinking. Render labels at least 9 points. None of the planned figures needs more than one panel per row.\n+\n+| Figure | Required design and evidence | Footprint and placement | Readability limits |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `score_prediction_overview` | One conceptual information-flow diagram: historical responses/full source scores → source-only shared subset design and decoder selection → legal target query answers → predicted full score; true retained target score remains beyond an external-scoring boundary. Mark nonlinear decoding optional/source-selected. Use `generate-concept-figure`. | Page 2, full 5.5-inch width; about 2.0-inch drawing height plus short caption, roughly 0.30 body page. Full width is necessary for legible matrix roles and information boundaries. | One panel, at most six blocks/categories, three visual information roles/series, at least 9-point labels. |\n+| `paired_error_comparison` | Horizontal forest plot of selected-minus-baseline MAE for uniform, prior, anchors, and IRT using the single supplied aggregate interval per comparator; common zero line. Generate with matplotlib. | Around page 6, full 5.5-inch width; about 1.7-inch axes height, roughly 0.26 body page with caption. Comparator labels, signed ticks, and intervals need the complete span. | One panel, four comparator categories, one series. Do not clip interval endpoints or duplicate the interval by seed. |\n+| `case_budget_reversals` | Two vertically stacked horizontal dot-plot panels: five leaderboard cases and four HELM cases. Each case has three offset budget symbols for candidate-minus-local-IRT MAE. Common signed x-axis; no connected progression lines. Generate with matplotlib. | Around page 7, full 5.5-inch width; about 3.2-inch total axes height, roughly 0.43 body page with caption. Stacking avoids illegible adjacent mini-panels and preserves all failure cells. | Two panels, one per row; at most five cases and three budget series per panel; shapes plus color, at least 9-point labels. |\n+\n+Only the overview uses the concept-figure workflow; the downstream orchestrator, not this framing stage, owns its execution. Preserve editable source and vector exports when available. Quantitative figures must have reproducible source and **both PDF and PNG exports**, with PNG at 300 DPI. LaTeX references the PDF whenever one exists. For raster-only full-width placement, regenerate at **at least 2400 pixels wide**; any justified narrower/column raster-only placement needs at least 1200 pixels. A 300-DPI preview at 5.5 inches is not enough for the raster-only full-width rule. Never upscale an existing image.\n+\n+## Body Budget and Scientific Structure\n+\n+Target about **8.5 body pages**, excluding references and substantive Supplementary Information:\n+\n+| Material | Body allocation including its floats |\n+| --- | ---: |\n+| Title, abstract, introduction, early overview | 1.5 pages |\n+| Problem/estimand and focused related work | 1.0 page |\n+| Weighted acquisition, decoding, source-only tuning | 1.8 pages |\n+| Frozen data, fair protocol, baseline definitions | 1.1 pages |\n+| Aggregate uncertainty, ranking, case/budget reversals | 2.0 pages |\n+| Interpretation, limitations, conclusion | 1.1 pages |\n+\n+Suggested headings: **Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Score-Targeted Subset Prediction; Evaluation Protocol; Results** with subsections **Aggregate Accuracy and Conditional Uncertainty** and **Benchmark-Specific Reversals and Ranking; Scope and Limitations; Conclusion**.\n+\n+Spend available space on precise estimands, the acquisition/decoder equations, group weighting, fold-local refitting, baseline definitions, interpretation of failures, and uncertainty assumptions. Do not add unsupported ablations, inflated related work, repeated plots, or oversized graphics to fill pages. The venue requires 8–9 body pages; an eight-page body must have its final page at least 75% full, and a nine-page body must not overflow the body limit. Check final layout later, not by final-paper validation during framing.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+**Purpose:** add reproducibility and complete evidence disaggregation without hiding any essential result, reversal, or limitation. Later authoritative appendix rankings can add material here without retroactively changing this strategy.\n+\n+1. **Weighted Acquisition and Decoder Specification.** Full weighted covariance/conditional-gain and decoder equations, source-only tuning shortlists and group partitions, optional branch, clipping, and zero-budget/insufficient-group fallbacks. Ground in the inspected selected source tree linked to `final.evidence.episodes` and `final.qualification.status`. Clearly distinguish specification from ablation evidence.\n+2. **Frozen Data and Lineage/Content Provenance.** Pinned snapshot, rebuild script, retained columns, actual evaluated dimensions, grouping rules, hashes, and conservative ancestry/content limitations. Ground the evaluated data link in `final.evidence.episodes` and detail provenance from the local manifests. Do not substitute generic task-brief model counts.\n+3. **Complete Benchmark, Budget, and Seed Results.** Every non-replay normal cell and its four baseline prediction arrays; reproducible MAE/ranking extraction and reconciliation to the recorded final metrics. Newly derived baseline statistics are postprocessing, not new runs; no invented cell intervals. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.mae`, `final.metric.rmse`, `final.metric.spearman`, `final.metric.kendall`, and the four baseline `final.metric.*` entries.\n+4. **Paired Uncertainty and Observation Controls.** The single fixed-case bootstrap, checkpoint/seed retention, equal-case weights, evaluator missing-cell policy, recorded zero failed normal cells, and intervention/replay/duplicate-history definitions. A no-failure count is not a performance-success rate or universal validity certificate. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.constant_mae`, `final.metric.permuted_mae`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.status`.\n+5. **Reproduction and Evidence Boundaries.** Anonymized reconstruction/evaluation commands based on existing scripts and dependency/specification files, seeds/budgets, hashes, and an eventual script-to-table/figure mapping. Label unrerun commands truthfully, report CPU requirements as requirements, and give no unmeasured speedup or end-to-end time. Include the absence of component ablations/branch-selection diagnostics. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes` and all three `final.qualification.*` entries.\n+6. **LLM Usage.** The separately required venue section: precise documented roles in ideation, implementation, citation-query planning, framing, and eventual writing/figure assistance; distinguish evaluator measurements from agent-produced interpretation. Disclose actual verification, not fictitious human review. Framing used local inspection and existing-prediction postprocessing, not candidate execution. Link measurements to `final.evidence.episodes`; process roles come from the supplied task/memory provenance, which is not quantitative evidence.\n+\n+## Literature and Readiness Boundary\n+\n+The supplied bibliography is mostly off-topic. The retrieval log shows its quota was exhausted before the planned task-specific title queries; relevant source metadata does not imply source reading. Some existing foundational entries may be useful leads, such as `Derezinski2019BayesianED`, `Ravi2016ExperimentalDO`, and `Uto2020AGM`, but their exact relevance must be checked and they do not substitute for the permitted benchmark-prediction literature.\n+\n+Before final related-work writing, repair this gap using permitted direct-title sources from the task brief and focused unrelated foundational material, maintain citation provenance, and cite only genuinely consulted relevant works with actual BibTeX keys. Do not cite tangential engineering papers to reach a target count. This is a **citation-readiness prerequisite**, not a reason to invent a weaker or broader empirical story. This stage does not modify references or perform retrieval.\n+\n+Never infer or search for the prohibited paper'\"'s identity or expand citation networks toward it. If a later accidental encounter occurs, stop and document location and reading extent. This local-only framing stage identified no such encounter. Omit authors, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, personal links and internal URLs from the anonymous manuscript. Do not invent a venue checklist requirement absent supporting venue instructions.\n+\n+## Anti-Diary and Overclaim Guardrails\n+\n+Avoid headings **Search Progression; Campaign Phases; Milestones; First Valid Result; Iteration History; Experiment A / Experiment B; From Audit to Ridge to Nonlinear; Winning Configuration; Nonlinear Decoder Ablation; Universal Benchmark Prediction**.\n+\n+Avoid wording **we then tried; subsequent improvements; first valid result; next-best; later variants; state of the art; wins on every benchmark; proves generalization; leakage-free; the nonlinear component caused the gain; unbiased rankings; adaptive per-target acquisition**. Internal field names and pipeline labels listed in the JSON forbidden phrases are private bookkeeping, never visible metrics or prose recommendations.\n+\n+Do not conflate source-only fitting with complete validity; score error with ranking preservation; aggregate confidence with new-benchmark uncertainty; local baseline families with exact published systems; or an implemented optional module with a measured component gain. Anonymization, qualification facts, mixed results, and scientific limitations must survive later writing, review, audit, and revision.\n+\n+## Stage Boundary\n+\n+Deliver only \"'`paper_strategy.json` and this mirrored memo, with append-only memory updates. Do not create `paper.tex`, `claims_grounding.json`, figures, new experiments, or final-paper validation outputs. Validate strategy schema, source-ID existence, figure budgets, qualification preservation, and memo agreement only. No final paper has been drafted in this stage.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA paper_strategy.json\nA paper_strategy.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
